    "breadcrumb": "Catalog",
    "content": "All degrees offered by the Department of Computer Science (the Bachelor of Computer Science, the Bachelor of Cybersecurity, and the Bachelor of Artificial Intelligence) share a rigorous 2-year (4-semester) experience grounding students in the foundations of computer science. This sequence of courses draws upon research-backed practices in its design (see chapter 1), where students explore and extend real-world, complex production software systems (see chapter 3) leading to a capstone software development experience at the end of the second year.\nAfter that point, students have the option of specializing in Cybersecurity or AI Systems. These specializations are the Computer Science degree with a curated choice of electives – essentially, the student will earn both a Bachelor of Computer Science and a Bachelor in the specialization field with no additional coursework or cost than the Bachelor of Computer Science would require. Alternatively, the student can choose to instead forge their own path, using the flexibility of the Bachelor of Computer Science to select electives that best explore their interests and lead to the career they envision for themselves.\nThe two-year plan for completing the computing foundations appears below (note: it is possible and common for students to deviate from this strict schedule):",
    "description": "All degrees offered by the Department of Computer Science (the Bachelor of Computer Science, the Bachelor of Cybersecurity, and the Bachelor of Artificial Intelligence) share a rigorous 2-year (4-semester) experience grounding students in the foundations of computer science. This sequence of courses draws upon research-backed practices in its design (see chapter 1), where students explore and extend real-world, complex production software systems (see chapter 3) leading to a capstone software development experience at the end of the second year.",
